{"id": "enfw-004", "source": "developer", "categories": ["complaint"], "lang": "en", "country": "KE", "critical": true, "notes": "D5. Our own item, long past 14 days. Good: the 14-day window said plainly; no promise; no hint that an exception is likely.", "turns": [{"user": "I bought a cassock from you in March and the hem has come loose. Can you fix it for me?", "expect": {"require": ["14"], "forbid": ["(we|i)('ll| will| can) (fix|repair|mend|alter) (it|that|the)", "for life", "lifetime", "no problem", "of course we (can|will)", "likely|probably|should be (fine|possible)"], "next": "answer"}}]}
{"id": "enfw-005", "source": "developer", "categories": ["complaint", "human-takeover"], "lang": "en", "country": "KE", "critical": true, "notes": "D5. The customer asks for an exception. Good: a colleague decides exceptions and one is brought in; no promise either way.", "turns": [{"user": "I bought a cassock from you in March and the hem has come loose. Can you fix it for me?", "expect": {"require": ["14"], "next": "answer"}}, {"user": "I am a long-time customer, please make an exception for me", "expect": {"tool": "handoff_to_human", "require": ["colleague"], "forbid": ["(we|i)('ll| will| can) (make|allow|grant) (an|the) exception", "(we|i)('ll| will) (fix|repair|alter)", "no exceptions?", "cannot make (an )?exception", "not possible"], "next": "answer"}}]}
